        "original_id": "c0f41ac7-1787-52b1-a566-c608310da2c1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beyazıt Tower, Beyazıt Square, Istanbul, Turkey, Golden Horn\n- Organizations: Istanbul University, Ottoman Ministry of War\n- Concepts: fire-watch towers, miniature parks, seven hills of Istanbul, Forum Tauri\n\nFacts:\n- Constantine the Great built the city of Istanbul on the model of Rome across seven hills, and Beyazıt Tower stands on one of those hills.\n- Beyazıt Square in Istanbul was known as the Forum Tauri during the Roman period.\n- Beyazıt Tower is also named Seraskier Tower after the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Beyazıt Tower is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower in the courtyard of Istanbul University’s main campus in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Istanbul University’s main campus formerly served as the Ottoman Ministry of War.\n- Beyazıt Tower is located on Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Miniatürk is a miniature park on the north-eastern shore of the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.",
